        "content": "Based on the GitHub search results for repositories created between July 18-31, 2026, here are the notable projects related to persistent memory for AI agents:\n\n**lorekit** by mthines  \nTypeScript-based solution offering \"offline and remote\" persistent memory designed specifically for AI coding agents. The project appears to focus on memory retention without requiring cloud connectivity.\n\n**AgentMemory-Persistent-Memory-2026** by PremierFoundry  \nPython desktop application supporting Claude Code, Cursor, and Gemini CLI. Notable for claiming \"95.2% recall accuracy\" and operating without API keys. Marketed as a productivity tool for AI agents.\n\n**engram-mcp** by lalithbuilds  \nDescribed as a \"Zero-dependency MCP server\" using pure Python standard library with SQLite. Notable for its emphasis on being entirely local—\"No cloud. No Docker. No API costs.\"\n\n**persistent-memory-agent-agno** by tirth1263  \nBuilt on the Agno framework with Nebius AI, this project emphasizes memory continuity \"across turns, sessions, and process restarts\" using SQLite as the storage backend.\n\n**JARVIS-AI-OS** by Vishwajeetsrk  \nA broader \"Persistent-memory AI OS\" incorporating 30 agents, voice assistance, and file creation capabilities for documents including Word, PowerPoint, and Excel files.\n\n**Persistent_Memory_Agent** by notayannn  \nUses Mem0 to power an AI chatbot called Jared, focusing on delivering personalized responses through persistent user memory storage.\n\nThe majority of these projects use Python as the primary language, with SQLite being a common choice for local storage, reflecting a trend toward self-hosted, API-free memory solutions."
